# --- Terraform: what never gets committed, and why ---

# The provider plugins terraform init downloads (~hundreds of MB).
# Recreatable anywhere by running init again.
.terraform/

# STATE. terraform.tfstate is Terraform's memory of everything it built,
# real resource IDs, full configuration values, and (in real projects)
# secrets in PLAINTEXT. It is never code; it is a live database of your
# environment. Committing it leaks data AND invites two people applying
# against different memories of the same infrastructure. Never commit it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Real variable values (per-person / per-env / secrets).
# The committed *.example shows the shape; the real file stays local.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars

# Crash logs and plan files (plans can embed sensitive values too).
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfplan

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored, it pins the exact
# provider version so every machine builds with the same plugin. Commit it.
